# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Secrets — .env holds the live database password and must never
# be committed. Only .env.example (the template) belongs in git.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build artefacts
build/
dist/

# Screenshots are committed deliberately: the brief requires
# screenshots in the repository. Large binaries are still ignored.
*.tmp
*.bak
# Text dump of the assignment brief produced by an external tool (not
# part of this project). Present on disk but deliberately untracked.
docs/assignment.txt

# Session handoff brief. Written for the benefit of another agent, not
# part of the deliverable, and it describes unfinished work.
HANDOFF.md
.neon
node_modules/

# Rewrite scaffolding for the JavaScript/TypeScript port. Generated by
# scripts/export_port.py, which reads the Python source and copies every
# SQL statement into port/sql/ with a function-by-function checklist in
# port/PORT_MAP.md. Nothing in the Python app depends on it and nothing
# in it is part of the graded deliverable, so it stays untracked and can
# be deleted freely. Regenerate with:
#     python scripts/export_port.py
port/

# Neon Functions scaffold. Not part of the deliverable.
#
# The course project is a Python/Streamlit application. neon.ts,
# hello.ts and package.json configure Neon *Functions* (serverless
# TypeScript) and Neon Auth, neither of which this application uses.
# They are kept on disk because they are a working deployment, but
# committing them to a graded repository would misrepresent what the
# project is. The PostgreSQL database they point at IS used, and is
# reached through DATABASE_URL alone.
neon.ts
hello.ts
package.json
package-lock.json
